    {
      "id": "n09-00",
      "name": "Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -380
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1300,
        "height": 240,
        "content": "## PRQA 09 · Label-Triggered Pipeline (Kiramido1/Amenly-Product)\nEvery minute: **Discover** open PRs labelled `to be test` that were not tested at their head SHA → **Claim** (once per SHA, concurrency 1) → **Env + Context** (disposable API at the SHA) → **Groq Prompt in 3 stages** (scope → coverage → sections, each ≤ 5.5k tokens, released when the shared ledger has TPM capacity; validated between stages, assembled locally) → **Quality Gate** on the complete prompt (≥ 85, hard fails; a failed or rejected generation falls back to the reference prompt) → **Start OpenCode Run** (executor `local`: the OpenCode CLI on this machine, free GLM, bubblewrap-isolated, live terminal window; `sandbox`: grant → worker → launcher → container) → **Wait / Poll** → **Report + Cleanup + Discord**.\nA blocked stage cleans up and reports to Discord by itself. n8n holds only the bridge token and the inference-only prompt credential: no GitHub, provider, grant or Discord secret."
      }
    },
